    "synthesis": "In-sample temperature scaling yielded T < 1.0 (T=0.5795 in Fold 1; T=0.6688 in Fold 2), artificially sharpening logits due to in-sample overfitting. In 2022 (when new ground-effect regulations emerged), this in-sample overconfidence severely penalized pure ML (w=1.00 loss blew up to 2.1853). Under the honest out-of-fold calibration (T=0.9385 for Fold 1; T=1.1603 for Fold 2) or uncalibrated softmax (T=1.0), pure ML in 2022 improves substantially to 1.6913 (OOF) and 1.6671 (T=1.0). Critically, candidate w=0.20 remains robust across all temperature regimes: in 2022 it achieves LL=1.7182 (OOF) vs baseline 1.8374; in 2023 it achieves LL=1.2048 (OOF) vs baseline 1.5401. Candidate w=0.20 consistently outperforms the empirical baseline regardless of calibration method."
  },
